[[:db/add "d9dc6910-635d-50c4-b176-6fbb2ac614b5" :answer/id #uuid "d9dc6910-635d-50c4-b176-6fbb2ac614b5"] [:db/add "d9dc6910-635d-50c4-b176-6fbb2ac614b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "d9dc6910-635d-50c4-b176-6fbb2ac614b5" :answer/value "Q(t)=25.2-21.2e^{-t/35}"] [:db/ensure "d9dc6910-635d-50c4-b176-6fbb2ac614b5" :answer/validate] [:db/add "67f70dc6-1daf-5923-90ad-76fd65eed828" :answer/id #uuid "67f70dc6-1daf-5923-90ad-76fd65eed828"] [:db/add "67f70dc6-1daf-5923-90ad-76fd65eed828" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "67f70dc6-1daf-5923-90ad-76fd65eed828" :answer/value "Q(t)=25.2-20.2e^{-t/35}"] [:db/ensure "67f70dc6-1daf-5923-90ad-76fd65eed828" :answer/validate] [:db/add "996a9731-acc5-5b69-8d22-f2fd2ac623d4" :answer/id #uuid "996a9731-acc5-5b69-8d22-f2fd2ac623d4"] [:db/add "996a9731-acc5-5b69-8d22-f2fd2ac623d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "996a9731-acc5-5b69-8d22-f2fd2ac623d4" :answer/value "Q(t)=25.2-20.2e^{-t/14}"] [:db/ensure "996a9731-acc5-5b69-8d22-f2fd2ac623d4" :answer/validate] [:db/add "ae638f6f-9aab-5257-8412-79161e72772d" :answer/id #uuid "ae638f6f-9aab-5257-8412-79161e72772d"] [:db/add "ae638f6f-9aab-5257-8412-79161e72772d" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "ae638f6f-9aab-5257-8412-79161e72772d" :answer/value "Q(t)=8.4-3.4e^{-t/35}"] [:db/ensure "ae638f6f-9aab-5257-8412-79161e72772d" :answer/validate] [:db/add "44b353c1-c2ee-54c3-b666-ccb5c859c5f6" :answer/id #uuid "44b353c1-c2ee-54c3-b666-ccb5c859c5f6"] [:db/add "44b353c1-c2ee-54c3-b666-ccb5c859c5f6" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "44b353c1-c2ee-54c3-b666-ccb5c859c5f6" :answer/value "Q(t)=8.4-4.4e^{-t/14}"] [:db/ensure "44b353c1-c2ee-54c3-b666-ccb5c859c5f6" :answer/validate] [:db/add "23514375-6fae-594a-b5a7-0e55f8d76eee" :answer-field/id #uuid "23514375-6fae-594a-b5a7-0e55f8d76eee"] [:db/add "23514375-6fae-594a-b5a7-0e55f8d76eee" :answer-field/key "selection"] [:db/add "23514375-6fae-594a-b5a7-0e55f8d76eee" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] [:db/add "23514375-6fae-594a-b5a7-0e55f8d76eee" :answer-field/choices "d9dc6910-635d-50c4-b176-6fbb2ac614b5"] [:db/add "23514375-6fae-594a-b5a7-0e55f8d76eee" :answer-field/choices "67f70dc6-1daf-5923-90ad-76fd65eed828"] [:db/add "23514375-6fae-594a-b5a7-0e55f8d76eee" :answer-field/choices "996a9731-acc5-5b69-8d22-f2fd2ac623d4"] [:db/add "23514375-6fae-594a-b5a7-0e55f8d76eee" :answer-field/choices "ae638f6f-9aab-5257-8412-79161e72772d"] [:db/add "23514375-6fae-594a-b5a7-0e55f8d76eee" :answer-field/choices "44b353c1-c2ee-54c3-b666-ccb5c859c5f6"] [:db/add "23514375-6fae-594a-b5a7-0e55f8d76eee" :answer-field/correct "44b353c1-c2ee-54c3-b666-ccb5c859c5f6"] [:db/ensure "23514375-6fae-594a-b5a7-0e55f8d76eee" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "d3e93811-bde2-50b4-a162-641048dbfc47" :question/id #uuid "d3e93811-bde2-50b4-a162-641048dbfc47"] [:db/add "d3e93811-bde2-50b4-a162-641048dbfc47" :question/problem "A coolant tank initially holds $420\\,\\text{L}$ of liquid containing $4\\,\\text{kg}$ of dissolved additive.\nA feed solution containing $0.02\\,\\text{kg/L}$ of the additive is pumped into the tank at a rate of $30\\,\\text{L/min},$ while the completely mixed liquid is drained out at a rate of $30\\,\\text{L/min}.$ Which expression gives the amount of additive $Q(t),$ in kilograms, in the tank $t$ minutes after pumping begins?"] [:db/add "d3e93811-bde2-50b4-a162-641048dbfc47" :question/worked-solution "Let $Q$ be the amount of additive in the tank at time $t,$ in minutes. Then, the derivative \n\n$$\n\\frac{dQ}{dt}\n$$\n\ndescribes how this amount changes with respect to time $t.$ This is equal to the rate at which additive enters the tank minus the rate at which additive leaves the tank.\n\n$$\n\\frac{dQ}{dt}={Q}_{\\text{in}}^{′}-{Q}_{\\text{out}}^{′}\n$$\n\nNote that the units of $\\frac{dQ}{dt},{Q}_{\\text{in}}^{′}$ and ${Q}_{\\text{out}}^{′}$ are $\\text{kg}/\\text{min}.$ Now, let's compute the required rates of change in steps.\n\n**Step 1**: Calculating the rate at which additive enters the tank.\n\nNote that a feed solution containing $0.02\\,\\text{kg/L}$ of the additive enters the tank at a rate of $30\\,\\text{L/min}.$ So, the rate at which the *additive* enters the tank is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Q}_{\\text{in}}^{′} & =(0.02\\,\\frac{\\text{kg}}{\\text{L}})\\cdot (30\\,\\frac{\\text{L}}{\\text{min}}) \\\\  & =(0.02\\,\\frac{\\text{kg}}{\\cancel{\\text{L}}})\\cdot (30\\,\\frac{\\cancel{\\text{L}}}{\\text{min}}) \\\\  & =0.6\\,\\frac{\\text{kg}}{\\text{min}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Calculating the rate at which additive exits the tank.\n\nNext, note that the rate of flow in equals the rate of flow out, so the volume in the tank remains $420\\,\\text{L}.$ Then, since $Q$ is the amount of additive in the tank, the *concentration* of the solution at time $t$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{Q}{420}\\,\\text{kg/L}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, as the completely mixed liquid leaves at a rate of $30\\,\\text{L/min},$ *additive* leaves at a rate of\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Q}_{\\text{out}}^{′} & =(30\\,\\frac{\\text{L}}{\\text{min}})\\cdot (\\frac{Q}{420}\\,\\frac{\\text{kg}}{\\text{L}}) \\\\  & =(30\\,\\frac{\\cancel{\\text{L}}}{\\text{min}})\\cdot (\\frac{Q}{420}\\,\\frac{\\text{kg}}{\\cancel{\\text{L}}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{30Q}{420}\\,\\frac{\\text{kg}}{\\text{min}} \\\\  & =\\frac{Q}{14}\\,\\frac{\\text{kg}}{\\text{min}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Calculate the overall rate of change.\n\nThe rate of change equals the rate of entry minus the rate of exit. Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dQ}{dt} & ={Q}_{\\text{in}}^{′}-{Q}_{\\text{out}}^{′} \\\\  & =0.6-\\frac{Q}{14}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dQ}{dt}+\\frac{1}{14}Q=0.6.\n$$\n\n**Step 4**: Integrate the equation.\n\nThis is a first-order linear equation with constant coefficients. To find the general solution, we must sum the complementary and particular solutions.\n\n- To find the complementary solution ${Q}_{c},$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{d{Q}_{c}}{dt}+\\frac{1}{14}{Q}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving using an integration technique, such as separation of variables, we obtain the complementary solution\n\n$$\n{Q}_{c}(t)=A{e}^{-t/14},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is a constant of integration.\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Note that the right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is a polynomial of degree $0.$ So, we assume that the particular solution is also a polynomial of degree $0,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{Q}_{p}(t)=\\alpha .\n$$\n\nTo find the value of $\\alpha ,$ we substitute ${Q}_{p}=\\alpha $ and $\\frac{d{Q}_{p}}{dt}=(\\alpha )^{′}=0$ into the inhomogeneous equation:\n\n$$\n0+\\frac{1}{14}\\alpha =0.6\\,⟹\\,\\alpha =8.4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution is ${Q}_{p}(t)=8.4.$\n\nNow, since the general solution is given by the sum of the complementary solution and the particular solution, the general solution in our case is\n\n$$\nQ(t)={Q}_{c}(t)+{Q}_{p}(t)=A{e}^{-t/14}+8.4.\n$$\n\nWe're told that the tank initially contains $4\\,\\text{kg}$ of dissolved additive. So, we can apply the initial condition $Q(0)=4,$ and solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(0) & =4 \\\\ A{e}^{-0/14}+8.4 & =4 \\\\ A & =-4.4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following expression for $Q(t):$\n\n$$\nQ(t)=8.4-4.4{e}^{-t/14}.\n$$"] [:db/add "d3e93811-bde2-50b4-a162-641048dbfc47" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] [:db/add "d3e93811-bde2-50b4-a162-641048dbfc47" :question/answer-fields "23514375-6fae-594a-b5a7-0e55f8d76eee"] [:db/ensure "d3e93811-bde2-50b4-a162-641048dbfc47" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186229181 :knowledge-point/questions "d3e93811-bde2-50b4-a162-641048dbfc47"] [:db/add "4a75fa10-6da7-5407-9c8d-f142fc65c9f9" :answer/id #uuid "4a75fa10-6da7-5407-9c8d-f142fc65c9f9"] [:db/add "4a75fa10-6da7-5407-9c8d-f142fc65c9f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "4a75fa10-6da7-5407-9c8d-f142fc65c9f9" :answer/value "Q(t)=18-8e^{-t/24}"] [:db/ensure "4a75fa10-6da7-5407-9c8d-f142fc65c9f9" :answer/validate] [:db/add "d583b770-9481-5579-8d91-684112cd4467" :answer/id #uuid "d583b770-9481-5579-8d91-684112cd4467"] [:db/add "d583b770-9481-5579-8d91-684112cd4467" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "d583b770-9481-5579-8d91-684112cd4467" :answer/value "Q(t)=18-12e^{-t/24}"] [:db/ensure "d583b770-9481-5579-8d91-684112cd4467" :answer/validate] [:db/add "4cf6c63e-69eb-5222-be8b-10c3f1be8e3b" :answer/id #uuid "4cf6c63e-69eb-5222-be8b-10c3f1be8e3b"] [:db/add "4cf6c63e-69eb-5222-be8b-10c3f1be8e3b" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "4cf6c63e-69eb-5222-be8b-10c3f1be8e3b" :answer/value "Q(t)=18-8e^{-t/30}"] [:db/ensure "4cf6c63e-69eb-5222-be8b-10c3f1be8e3b" :answer/validate] [:db/add "247aea16-5a0e-53c2-9eab-769593e0321b" :answer/id #uuid "247aea16-5a0e-53c2-9eab-769593e0321b"] [:db/add "247aea16-5a0e-53c2-9eab-769593e0321b" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "247aea16-5a0e-53c2-9eab-769593e0321b" :answer/value "Q(t)=10.8-4.8e^{-t/30}"] [:db/ensure "247aea16-5a0e-53c2-9eab-769593e0321b" :answer/validate] [:db/add "9294db4d-c049-5c7e-9775-3e4ab32bdfb2" :answer/id #uuid "9294db4d-c049-5c7e-9775-3e4ab32bdfb2"] [:db/add "9294db4d-c049-5c7e-9775-3e4ab32bdfb2" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "9294db4d-c049-5c7e-9775-3e4ab32bdfb2" :answer/value "Q(t)=10.8-0.8e^{-t/24}"] [:db/ensure "9294db4d-c049-5c7e-9775-3e4ab32bdfb2" :answer/validate] [:db/add "f72c24e8-2705-5501-b569-59c87bcb3ce2" :answer-field/id #uuid "f72c24e8-2705-5501-b569-59c87bcb3ce2"] [:db/add "f72c24e8-2705-5501-b569-59c87bcb3ce2" :answer-field/key "selection"] [:db/add "f72c24e8-2705-5501-b569-59c87bcb3ce2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] [:db/add "f72c24e8-2705-5501-b569-59c87bcb3ce2" :answer-field/choices "4a75fa10-6da7-5407-9c8d-f142fc65c9f9"] [:db/add "f72c24e8-2705-5501-b569-59c87bcb3ce2" :answer-field/choices "d583b770-9481-5579-8d91-684112cd4467"] [:db/add "f72c24e8-2705-5501-b569-59c87bcb3ce2" :answer-field/choices "4cf6c63e-69eb-5222-be8b-10c3f1be8e3b"] [:db/add "f72c24e8-2705-5501-b569-59c87bcb3ce2" :answer-field/choices "247aea16-5a0e-53c2-9eab-769593e0321b"] [:db/add "f72c24e8-2705-5501-b569-59c87bcb3ce2" :answer-field/choices "9294db4d-c049-5c7e-9775-3e4ab32bdfb2"] [:db/add "f72c24e8-2705-5501-b569-59c87bcb3ce2" :answer-field/correct "247aea16-5a0e-53c2-9eab-769593e0321b"] [:db/ensure "f72c24e8-2705-5501-b569-59c87bcb3ce2" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "1b80a0f4-7801-535e-bc20-eae6ddee5773" :question/id #uuid "1b80a0f4-7801-535e-bc20-eae6ddee5773"] [:db/add "1b80a0f4-7801-535e-bc20-eae6ddee5773" :question/problem "A brewing tank initially holds $360\\,\\text{L}$ of liquid containing $6\\,\\text{kg}$ of dissolved sugar.\nA feed solution containing $0.03\\,\\text{kg/L}$ of the sugar is pumped into the tank at a rate of $12\\,\\text{L/min},$ while the completely mixed liquid is drained out at a rate of $12\\,\\text{L/min}.$ Which expression gives the amount of sugar $Q(t),$ in kilograms, in the tank $t$ minutes after pumping begins?"] [:db/add "1b80a0f4-7801-535e-bc20-eae6ddee5773" :question/worked-solution "Let $Q$ be the amount of sugar in the tank at time $t,$ in minutes. Then, the derivative \n\n$$\n\\frac{dQ}{dt}\n$$\n\ndescribes how this amount changes with respect to time $t.$ This is equal to the rate at which sugar enters the tank minus the rate at which sugar leaves the tank.\n\n$$\n\\frac{dQ}{dt}={Q}_{\\text{in}}^{′}-{Q}_{\\text{out}}^{′}\n$$\n\nNote that the units of $\\frac{dQ}{dt},{Q}_{\\text{in}}^{′}$ and ${Q}_{\\text{out}}^{′}$ are $\\text{kg}/\\text{min}.$ Now, let's compute the required rates of change in steps.\n\n**Step 1**: Calculating the rate at which sugar enters the tank.\n\nNote that a feed solution containing $0.03\\,\\text{kg/L}$ of the sugar enters the tank at a rate of $12\\,\\text{L/min}.$ So, the rate at which the *sugar* enters the tank is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Q}_{\\text{in}}^{′} & =(0.03\\,\\frac{\\text{kg}}{\\text{L}})\\cdot (12\\,\\frac{\\text{L}}{\\text{min}}) \\\\  & =(0.03\\,\\frac{\\text{kg}}{\\cancel{\\text{L}}})\\cdot (12\\,\\frac{\\cancel{\\text{L}}}{\\text{min}}) \\\\  & =0.36\\,\\frac{\\text{kg}}{\\text{min}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Calculating the rate at which sugar exits the tank.\n\nNext, note that the rate of flow in equals the rate of flow out, so the volume in the tank remains $360\\,\\text{L}.$ Then, since $Q$ is the amount of sugar in the tank, the *concentration* of the solution at time $t$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{Q}{360}\\,\\text{kg/L}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, as the completely mixed liquid leaves at a rate of $12\\,\\text{L/min},$ *sugar* leaves at a rate of\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Q}_{\\text{out}}^{′} & =(12\\,\\frac{\\text{L}}{\\text{min}})\\cdot (\\frac{Q}{360}\\,\\frac{\\text{kg}}{\\text{L}}) \\\\  & =(12\\,\\frac{\\cancel{\\text{L}}}{\\text{min}})\\cdot (\\frac{Q}{360}\\,\\frac{\\text{kg}}{\\cancel{\\text{L}}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{12Q}{360}\\,\\frac{\\text{kg}}{\\text{min}} \\\\  & =\\frac{Q}{30}\\,\\frac{\\text{kg}}{\\text{min}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Calculate the overall rate of change.\n\nThe rate of change equals the rate of entry minus the rate of exit. Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dQ}{dt} & ={Q}_{\\text{in}}^{′}-{Q}_{\\text{out}}^{′} \\\\  & =0.36-\\frac{Q}{30}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dQ}{dt}+\\frac{1}{30}Q=0.36.\n$$\n\n**Step 4**: Integrate the equation.\n\nThis is a first-order linear equation with constant coefficients. To find the general solution, we must sum the complementary and particular solutions.\n\n- To find the complementary solution ${Q}_{c},$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{d{Q}_{c}}{dt}+\\frac{1}{30}{Q}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving using an integration technique, such as separation of variables, we obtain the complementary solution\n\n$$\n{Q}_{c}(t)=A{e}^{-t/30},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is a constant of integration.\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Note that the right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is a polynomial of degree $0.$ So, we assume that the particular solution is also a polynomial of degree $0,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{Q}_{p}(t)=\\alpha .\n$$\n\nTo find the value of $\\alpha ,$ we substitute ${Q}_{p}=\\alpha $ and $\\frac{d{Q}_{p}}{dt}=(\\alpha )^{′}=0$ into the inhomogeneous equation:\n\n$$\n0+\\frac{1}{30}\\alpha =0.36\\,⟹\\,\\alpha =10.8.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution is ${Q}_{p}(t)=10.8.$\n\nNow, since the general solution is given by the sum of the complementary solution and the particular solution, the general solution in our case is\n\n$$\nQ(t)={Q}_{c}(t)+{Q}_{p}(t)=A{e}^{-t/30}+10.8.\n$$\n\nWe're told that the tank initially contains $6\\,\\text{kg}$ of dissolved sugar. So, we can apply the initial condition $Q(0)=6,$ and solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(0) & =6 \\\\ A{e}^{-0/30}+10.8 & =6 \\\\ A & =-4.8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following expression for $Q(t):$\n\n$$\nQ(t)=10.8-4.8{e}^{-t/30}.\n$$"] [:db/add "1b80a0f4-7801-535e-bc20-eae6ddee5773" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] [:db/add "1b80a0f4-7801-535e-bc20-eae6ddee5773" :question/answer-fields "f72c24e8-2705-5501-b569-59c87bcb3ce2"] [:db/ensure "1b80a0f4-7801-535e-bc20-eae6ddee5773" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186229181 :knowledge-point/questions "1b80a0f4-7801-535e-bc20-eae6ddee5773"] [:db/add "2672e6b2-eafa-5b83-9c60-d31c4e3baaed" :answer/id #uuid "2672e6b2-eafa-5b83-9c60-d31c4e3baaed"] [:db/add "2672e6b2-eafa-5b83-9c60-d31c4e3baaed" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "2672e6b2-eafa-5b83-9c60-d31c4e3baaed" :answer/value "Q(t)=14-2e^{-t/35}"] [:db/ensure "2672e6b2-eafa-5b83-9c60-d31c4e3baaed" :answer/validate] [:db/add "f524c191-98bd-54bf-8c61-18cfacadfeed" :answer/id #uuid "f524c191-98bd-54bf-8c61-18cfacadfeed"] [:db/add "f524c191-98bd-54bf-8c61-18cfacadfeed" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "f524c191-98bd-54bf-8c61-18cfacadfeed" :answer/value "Q(t)=21-9e^{-t/14}"] [:db/ensure "f524c191-98bd-54bf-8c61-18cfacadfeed" :answer/validate] [:db/add "5f6606fe-295f-54d9-a96b-ece95eaa67cb" :answer/id #uuid "5f6606fe-295f-54d9-a96b-ece95eaa67cb"] [:db/add "5f6606fe-295f-54d9-a96b-ece95eaa67cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "5f6606fe-295f-54d9-a96b-ece95eaa67cb" :answer/value "Q(t)=21-3e^{-t/35}"] [:db/ensure "5f6606fe-295f-54d9-a96b-ece95eaa67cb" :answer/validate] [:db/add "a57aeafe-7041-5c00-8fd6-c39c93acb22f" :answer/id #uuid "a57aeafe-7041-5c00-8fd6-c39c93acb22f"] [:db/add "a57aeafe-7041-5c00-8fd6-c39c93acb22f" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "a57aeafe-7041-5c00-8fd6-c39c93acb22f" :answer/value "Q(t)=14+4e^{-t/14}"] [:db/ensure "a57aeafe-7041-5c00-8fd6-c39c93acb22f" :answer/validate] [:db/add "a7e7feec-a4a9-5925-8994-9b16f6261677" :answer/id #uuid "a7e7feec-a4a9-5925-8994-9b16f6261677"] [:db/add "a7e7feec-a4a9-5925-8994-9b16f6261677" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "a7e7feec-a4a9-5925-8994-9b16f6261677" :answer/value "Q(t)=21-3e^{-t/14}"] [:db/ensure "a7e7feec-a4a9-5925-8994-9b16f6261677" :answer/validate] [:db/add "669474bd-f365-5bcf-8161-9f793e84c972" :answer-field/id #uuid "669474bd-f365-5bcf-8161-9f793e84c972"] [:db/add "669474bd-f365-5bcf-8161-9f793e84c972" :answer-field/key "selection"] [:db/add "669474bd-f365-5bcf-8161-9f793e84c972" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] [:db/add "669474bd-f365-5bcf-8161-9f793e84c972" :answer-field/choices "2672e6b2-eafa-5b83-9c60-d31c4e3baaed"] [:db/add "669474bd-f365-5bcf-8161-9f793e84c972" :answer-field/choices "f524c191-98bd-54bf-8c61-18cfacadfeed"] [:db/add "669474bd-f365-5bcf-8161-9f793e84c972" :answer-field/choices "5f6606fe-295f-54d9-a96b-ece95eaa67cb"] [:db/add "669474bd-f365-5bcf-8161-9f793e84c972" :answer-field/choices "a57aeafe-7041-5c00-8fd6-c39c93acb22f"] [:db/add "669474bd-f365-5bcf-8161-9f793e84c972" :answer-field/choices "a7e7feec-a4a9-5925-8994-9b16f6261677"] [:db/add "669474bd-f365-5bcf-8161-9f793e84c972" :answer-field/correct "a7e7feec-a4a9-5925-8994-9b16f6261677"] [:db/ensure "669474bd-f365-5bcf-8161-9f793e84c972" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "387eb92e-520a-5684-94a0-8f6b898f8d01" :question/id #uuid "387eb92e-520a-5684-94a0-8f6b898f8d01"] [:db/add "387eb92e-520a-5684-94a0-8f6b898f8d01" :question/problem "A storage tank initially holds $350\\,\\text{L}$ of liquid containing $18\\,\\text{kg}$ of dissolved disinfectant.\nA feed solution containing $0.06\\,\\text{kg/L}$ of the disinfectant is pumped into the tank at a rate of $25\\,\\text{L/min},$ while the completely mixed liquid is drained out at a rate of $25\\,\\text{L/min}.$ Which expression gives the amount of disinfectant $Q(t),$ in kilograms, in the tank $t$ minutes after pumping begins?"] [:db/add "387eb92e-520a-5684-94a0-8f6b898f8d01" :question/worked-solution "Let $Q$ be the amount of disinfectant in the tank at time $t,$ in minutes. Then, the derivative \n\n$$\n\\frac{dQ}{dt}\n$$\n\ndescribes how this amount changes with respect to time $t.$ This is equal to the rate at which disinfectant enters the tank minus the rate at which disinfectant leaves the tank.\n\n$$\n\\frac{dQ}{dt}={Q}_{\\text{in}}^{′}-{Q}_{\\text{out}}^{′}\n$$\n\nNote that the units of $\\frac{dQ}{dt},{Q}_{\\text{in}}^{′}$ and ${Q}_{\\text{out}}^{′}$ are $\\text{kg}/\\text{min}.$ Now, let's compute the required rates of change in steps.\n\n**Step 1**: Calculating the rate at which disinfectant enters the tank.\n\nNote that a feed solution containing $0.06\\,\\text{kg/L}$ of the disinfectant enters the tank at a rate of $25\\,\\text{L/min}.$ So, the rate at which the *disinfectant* enters the tank is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Q}_{\\text{in}}^{′} & =(0.06\\,\\frac{\\text{kg}}{\\text{L}})\\cdot (25\\,\\frac{\\text{L}}{\\text{min}}) \\\\  & =(0.06\\,\\frac{\\text{kg}}{\\cancel{\\text{L}}})\\cdot (25\\,\\frac{\\cancel{\\text{L}}}{\\text{min}}) \\\\  & =1.5\\,\\frac{\\text{kg}}{\\text{min}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Calculating the rate at which disinfectant exits the tank.\n\nNext, note that the rate of flow in equals the rate of flow out, so the volume in the tank remains $350\\,\\text{L}.$ Then, since $Q$ is the amount of disinfectant in the tank, the *concentration* of the solution at time $t$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{Q}{350}\\,\\text{kg/L}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, as the completely mixed liquid leaves at a rate of $25\\,\\text{L/min},$ *disinfectant* leaves at a rate of\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Q}_{\\text{out}}^{′} & =(25\\,\\frac{\\text{L}}{\\text{min}})\\cdot (\\frac{Q}{350}\\,\\frac{\\text{kg}}{\\text{L}}) \\\\  & =(25\\,\\frac{\\cancel{\\text{L}}}{\\text{min}})\\cdot (\\frac{Q}{350}\\,\\frac{\\text{kg}}{\\cancel{\\text{L}}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{25Q}{350}\\,\\frac{\\text{kg}}{\\text{min}} \\\\  & =\\frac{Q}{14}\\,\\frac{\\text{kg}}{\\text{min}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Calculate the overall rate of change.\n\nThe rate of change equals the rate of entry minus the rate of exit. Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dQ}{dt} & ={Q}_{\\text{in}}^{′}-{Q}_{\\text{out}}^{′} \\\\  & =1.5-\\frac{Q}{14}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dQ}{dt}+\\frac{1}{14}Q=1.5.\n$$\n\n**Step 4**: Integrate the equation.\n\nThis is a first-order linear equation with constant coefficients. To find the general solution, we must sum the complementary and particular solutions.\n\n- To find the complementary solution ${Q}_{c},$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{d{Q}_{c}}{dt}+\\frac{1}{14}{Q}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving using an integration technique, such as separation of variables, we obtain the complementary solution\n\n$$\n{Q}_{c}(t)=A{e}^{-t/14},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is a constant of integration.\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Note that the right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is a polynomial of degree $0.$ So, we assume that the particular solution is also a polynomial of degree $0,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{Q}_{p}(t)=\\alpha .\n$$\n\nTo find the value of $\\alpha ,$ we substitute ${Q}_{p}=\\alpha $ and $\\frac{d{Q}_{p}}{dt}=(\\alpha )^{′}=0$ into the inhomogeneous equation:\n\n$$\n0+\\frac{1}{14}\\alpha =1.5\\,⟹\\,\\alpha =21.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution is ${Q}_{p}(t)=21.$\n\nNow, since the general solution is given by the sum of the complementary solution and the particular solution, the general solution in our case is\n\n$$\nQ(t)={Q}_{c}(t)+{Q}_{p}(t)=A{e}^{-t/14}+21.\n$$\n\nWe're told that the tank initially contains $18\\,\\text{kg}$ of dissolved disinfectant. So, we can apply the initial condition $Q(0)=18,$ and solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(0) & =18 \\\\ A{e}^{-0/14}+21 & =18 \\\\ A & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following expression for $Q(t):$\n\n$$\nQ(t)=21-3{e}^{-t/14}.\n$$"] [:db/add "387eb92e-520a-5684-94a0-8f6b898f8d01" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] [:db/add "387eb92e-520a-5684-94a0-8f6b898f8d01" :question/answer-fields "669474bd-f365-5bcf-8161-9f793e84c972"] [:db/ensure "387eb92e-520a-5684-94a0-8f6b898f8d01" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186229181 :knowledge-point/questions "387eb92e-520a-5684-94a0-8f6b898f8d01"] [:db/add "91d23fe2-88cf-561c-a0e4-1741996358a3" :answer/id #uuid "91d23fe2-88cf-561c-a0e4-1741996358a3"] [:db/add "91d23fe2-88cf-561c-a0e4-1741996358a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "91d23fe2-88cf-561c-a0e4-1741996358a3" :answer/value "Q(t)=10+5e^{-t/25}"] [:db/ensure "91d23fe2-88cf-561c-a0e4-1741996358a3" :answer/validate] [:db/add "5f327130-ce5a-5579-9f17-3c81140d18c6" :answer/id #uuid "5f327130-ce5a-5579-9f17-3c81140d18c6"] [:db/add "5f327130-ce5a-5579-9f17-3c81140d18c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "5f327130-ce5a-5579-9f17-3c81140d18c6" :answer/value "Q(t)=60-46e^{-t/25}"] [:db/ensure "5f327130-ce5a-5579-9f17-3c81140d18c6" :answer/validate] [:db/add "9071fcc3-5fc2-5104-a059-5fc677809145" :answer/id #uuid "9071fcc3-5fc2-5104-a059-5fc677809145"] [:db/add "9071fcc3-5fc2-5104-a059-5fc677809145" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "9071fcc3-5fc2-5104-a059-5fc677809145" :answer/value "Q(t)=10+4e^{-t/40}"] [:db/ensure "9071fcc3-5fc2-5104-a059-5fc677809145" :answer/validate] [:db/add "f23c15db-b163-510c-9170-9872773ac7af" :answer/id #uuid "f23c15db-b163-510c-9170-9872773ac7af"] [:db/add "f23c15db-b163-510c-9170-9872773ac7af" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "f23c15db-b163-510c-9170-9872773ac7af" :answer/value "Q(t)=60-45e^{-t/40}"] [:db/ensure "f23c15db-b163-510c-9170-9872773ac7af" :answer/validate] [:db/add "ae63b870-5af2-55d8-954f-51150459ff29" :answer/id #uuid "ae63b870-5af2-55d8-954f-51150459ff29"] [:db/add "ae63b870-5af2-55d8-954f-51150459ff29" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "ae63b870-5af2-55d8-954f-51150459ff29" :answer/value "Q(t)=10+5e^{-t/40}"] [:db/ensure "ae63b870-5af2-55d8-954f-51150459ff29" :answer/validate] [:db/add "31456c23-1619-532c-936a-7b4aab6fde98" :answer-field/id #uuid "31456c23-1619-532c-936a-7b4aab6fde98"] [:db/add "31456c23-1619-532c-936a-7b4aab6fde98" :answer-field/key "selection"] [:db/add "31456c23-1619-532c-936a-7b4aab6fde98" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] [:db/add "31456c23-1619-532c-936a-7b4aab6fde98" :answer-field/choices "91d23fe2-88cf-561c-a0e4-1741996358a3"] [:db/add "31456c23-1619-532c-936a-7b4aab6fde98" :answer-field/choices "5f327130-ce5a-5579-9f17-3c81140d18c6"] [:db/add "31456c23-1619-532c-936a-7b4aab6fde98" :answer-field/choices "9071fcc3-5fc2-5104-a059-5fc677809145"] [:db/add "31456c23-1619-532c-936a-7b4aab6fde98" :answer-field/choices "f23c15db-b163-510c-9170-9872773ac7af"] [:db/add "31456c23-1619-532c-936a-7b4aab6fde98" :answer-field/choices "ae63b870-5af2-55d8-954f-51150459ff29"] [:db/add "31456c23-1619-532c-936a-7b4aab6fde98" :answer-field/correct "ae63b870-5af2-55d8-954f-51150459ff29"] [:db/ensure "31456c23-1619-532c-936a-7b4aab6fde98" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "bd866fe0-d825-5d93-8387-02823cb34e5f" :question/id #uuid "bd866fe0-d825-5d93-8387-02823cb34e5f"] [:db/add "bd866fe0-d825-5d93-8387-02823cb34e5f" :question/problem "A brewing tank initially holds $1000\\,\\text{L}$ of liquid containing $15\\,\\text{kg}$ of dissolved sugar.\nA feed solution containing $0.01\\,\\text{kg/L}$ of the sugar is pumped into the tank at a rate of $25\\,\\text{L/min},$ while the completely mixed liquid is drained out at a rate of $25\\,\\text{L/min}.$ Which expression gives the amount of sugar $Q(t),$ in kilograms, in the tank $t$ minutes after pumping begins?"] [:db/add "bd866fe0-d825-5d93-8387-02823cb34e5f" :question/worked-solution "Let $Q$ be the amount of sugar in the tank at time $t,$ in minutes. Then, the derivative \n\n$$\n\\frac{dQ}{dt}\n$$\n\ndescribes how this amount changes with respect to time $t.$ This is equal to the rate at which sugar enters the tank minus the rate at which sugar leaves the tank.\n\n$$\n\\frac{dQ}{dt}={Q}_{\\text{in}}^{′}-{Q}_{\\text{out}}^{′}\n$$\n\nNote that the units of $\\frac{dQ}{dt},{Q}_{\\text{in}}^{′}$ and ${Q}_{\\text{out}}^{′}$ are $\\text{kg}/\\text{min}.$ Now, let's compute the required rates of change in steps.\n\n**Step 1**: Calculating the rate at which sugar enters the tank.\n\nNote that a feed solution containing $0.01\\,\\text{kg/L}$ of the sugar enters the tank at a rate of $25\\,\\text{L/min}.$ So, the rate at which the *sugar* enters the tank is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Q}_{\\text{in}}^{′} & =(0.01\\,\\frac{\\text{kg}}{\\text{L}})\\cdot (25\\,\\frac{\\text{L}}{\\text{min}}) \\\\  & =(0.01\\,\\frac{\\text{kg}}{\\cancel{\\text{L}}})\\cdot (25\\,\\frac{\\cancel{\\text{L}}}{\\text{min}}) \\\\  & =0.25\\,\\frac{\\text{kg}}{\\text{min}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Calculating the rate at which sugar exits the tank.\n\nNext, note that the rate of flow in equals the rate of flow out, so the volume in the tank remains $1000\\,\\text{L}.$ Then, since $Q$ is the amount of sugar in the tank, the *concentration* of the solution at time $t$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{Q}{1000}\\,\\text{kg/L}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, as the completely mixed liquid leaves at a rate of $25\\,\\text{L/min},$ *sugar* leaves at a rate of\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Q}_{\\text{out}}^{′} & =(25\\,\\frac{\\text{L}}{\\text{min}})\\cdot (\\frac{Q}{1000}\\,\\frac{\\text{kg}}{\\text{L}}) \\\\  & =(25\\,\\frac{\\cancel{\\text{L}}}{\\text{min}})\\cdot (\\frac{Q}{1000}\\,\\frac{\\text{kg}}{\\cancel{\\text{L}}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{25Q}{1000}\\,\\frac{\\text{kg}}{\\text{min}} \\\\  & =\\frac{Q}{40}\\,\\frac{\\text{kg}}{\\text{min}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Calculate the overall rate of change.\n\nThe rate of change equals the rate of entry minus the rate of exit. Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dQ}{dt} & ={Q}_{\\text{in}}^{′}-{Q}_{\\text{out}}^{′} \\\\  & =0.25-\\frac{Q}{40}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dQ}{dt}+\\frac{1}{40}Q=0.25.\n$$\n\n**Step 4**: Integrate the equation.\n\nThis is a first-order linear equation with constant coefficients. To find the general solution, we must sum the complementary and particular solutions.\n\n- To find the complementary solution ${Q}_{c},$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{d{Q}_{c}}{dt}+\\frac{1}{40}{Q}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving using an integration technique, such as separation of variables, we obtain the complementary solution\n\n$$\n{Q}_{c}(t)=A{e}^{-t/40},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is a constant of integration.\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Note that the right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is a polynomial of degree $0.$ So, we assume that the particular solution is also a polynomial of degree $0,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{Q}_{p}(t)=\\alpha .\n$$\n\nTo find the value of $\\alpha ,$ we substitute ${Q}_{p}=\\alpha $ and $\\frac{d{Q}_{p}}{dt}=(\\alpha )^{′}=0$ into the inhomogeneous equation:\n\n$$\n0+\\frac{1}{40}\\alpha =0.25\\,⟹\\,\\alpha =10.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution is ${Q}_{p}(t)=10.$\n\nNow, since the general solution is given by the sum of the complementary solution and the particular solution, the general solution in our case is\n\n$$\nQ(t)={Q}_{c}(t)+{Q}_{p}(t)=A{e}^{-t/40}+10.\n$$\n\nWe're told that the tank initially contains $15\\,\\text{kg}$ of dissolved sugar. So, we can apply the initial condition $Q(0)=15,$ and solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(0) & =15 \\\\ A{e}^{-0/40}+10 & =15 \\\\ A & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following expression for $Q(t):$\n\n$$\nQ(t)=10+5{e}^{-t/40}.\n$$"] [:db/add "bd866fe0-d825-5d93-8387-02823cb34e5f" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] [:db/add "bd866fe0-d825-5d93-8387-02823cb34e5f" :question/answer-fields "31456c23-1619-532c-936a-7b4aab6fde98"] [:db/ensure "bd866fe0-d825-5d93-8387-02823cb34e5f" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186229181 :knowledge-point/questions "bd866fe0-d825-5d93-8387-02823cb34e5f"] [:db/add "e0be752c-5cae-56aa-a99b-5e2e3da84b7d" :answer/id #uuid "e0be752c-5cae-56aa-a99b-5e2e3da84b7d"] [:db/add "e0be752c-5cae-56aa-a99b-5e2e3da84b7d" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "e0be752c-5cae-56aa-a99b-5e2e3da84b7d" :answer/value "Q(t)=24-9e^{-t/80}"] [:db/ensure "e0be752c-5cae-56aa-a99b-5e2e3da84b7d" :answer/validate] [:db/add "4a120c58-a242-55df-ae6b-10b365f315f4" :answer/id #uuid "4a120c58-a242-55df-ae6b-10b365f315f4"] [:db/add "4a120c58-a242-55df-ae6b-10b365f315f4" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "4a120c58-a242-55df-ae6b-10b365f315f4" :answer/value "Q(t)=16-e^{-t/80}"] [:db/ensure "4a120c58-a242-55df-ae6b-10b365f315f4" :answer/validate] [:db/add "9d11c0ba-204a-532b-a292-0fbe25eff11e" :answer/id #uuid "9d11c0ba-204a-532b-a292-0fbe25eff11e"] [:db/add "9d11c0ba-204a-532b-a292-0fbe25eff11e" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "9d11c0ba-204a-532b-a292-0fbe25eff11e" :answer/value "Q(t)=24-9e^{-t/16}"] [:db/ensure "9d11c0ba-204a-532b-a292-0fbe25eff11e" :answer/validate] [:db/add "63be0667-c58b-5165-b1b6-6499626e2f24" :answer/id #uuid "63be0667-c58b-5165-b1b6-6499626e2f24"] [:db/add "63be0667-c58b-5165-b1b6-6499626e2f24" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "63be0667-c58b-5165-b1b6-6499626e2f24" :answer/value "Q(t)=16+9e^{-t/16}"] [:db/ensure "63be0667-c58b-5165-b1b6-6499626e2f24" :answer/validate] [:db/add "74120287-fbd3-5aed-838e-a58eb85a7813" :answer/id #uuid "74120287-fbd3-5aed-838e-a58eb85a7813"] [:db/add "74120287-fbd3-5aed-838e-a58eb85a7813" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "74120287-fbd3-5aed-838e-a58eb85a7813" :answer/value "Q(t)=24+e^{-t/80}"] [:db/ensure "74120287-fbd3-5aed-838e-a58eb85a7813" :answer/validate] [:db/add "4cab0c71-5a81-5ddc-9dfe-02c242f74b7b" :answer-field/id #uuid "4cab0c71-5a81-5ddc-9dfe-02c242f74b7b"] [:db/add "4cab0c71-5a81-5ddc-9dfe-02c242f74b7b" :answer-field/key "selection"] [:db/add "4cab0c71-5a81-5ddc-9dfe-02c242f74b7b" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] [:db/add "4cab0c71-5a81-5ddc-9dfe-02c242f74b7b" :answer-field/choices "e0be752c-5cae-56aa-a99b-5e2e3da84b7d"] [:db/add "4cab0c71-5a81-5ddc-9dfe-02c242f74b7b" :answer-field/choices "4a120c58-a242-55df-ae6b-10b365f315f4"] [:db/add "4cab0c71-5a81-5ddc-9dfe-02c242f74b7b" :answer-field/choices "9d11c0ba-204a-532b-a292-0fbe25eff11e"] [:db/add "4cab0c71-5a81-5ddc-9dfe-02c242f74b7b" :answer-field/choices "63be0667-c58b-5165-b1b6-6499626e2f24"] [:db/add "4cab0c71-5a81-5ddc-9dfe-02c242f74b7b" :answer-field/choices "74120287-fbd3-5aed-838e-a58eb85a7813"] [:db/add "4cab0c71-5a81-5ddc-9dfe-02c242f74b7b" :answer-field/correct "e0be752c-5cae-56aa-a99b-5e2e3da84b7d"] [:db/ensure "4cab0c71-5a81-5ddc-9dfe-02c242f74b7b" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "79b642d6-727a-5f0d-9531-4fcd626dce40" :question/id #uuid "79b642d6-727a-5f0d-9531-4fcd626dce40"] [:db/add "79b642d6-727a-5f0d-9531-4fcd626dce40" :question/problem "A coolant tank initially holds $800\\,\\text{L}$ of liquid containing $15\\,\\text{kg}$ of dissolved additive.\nA feed solution containing $0.03\\,\\text{kg/L}$ of the additive is pumped into the tank at a rate of $10\\,\\text{L/min},$ while the completely mixed liquid is drained out at a rate of $10\\,\\text{L/min}.$ Which expression gives the amount of additive $Q(t),$ in kilograms, in the tank $t$ minutes after pumping begins?"] [:db/add "79b642d6-727a-5f0d-9531-4fcd626dce40" :question/worked-solution "Let $Q$ be the amount of additive in the tank at time $t,$ in minutes. Then, the derivative \n\n$$\n\\frac{dQ}{dt}\n$$\n\ndescribes how this amount changes with respect to time $t.$ This is equal to the rate at which additive enters the tank minus the rate at which additive leaves the tank.\n\n$$\n\\frac{dQ}{dt}={Q}_{\\text{in}}^{′}-{Q}_{\\text{out}}^{′}\n$$\n\nNote that the units of $\\frac{dQ}{dt},{Q}_{\\text{in}}^{′}$ and ${Q}_{\\text{out}}^{′}$ are $\\text{kg}/\\text{min}.$ Now, let's compute the required rates of change in steps.\n\n**Step 1**: Calculating the rate at which additive enters the tank.\n\nNote that a feed solution containing $0.03\\,\\text{kg/L}$ of the additive enters the tank at a rate of $10\\,\\text{L/min}.$ So, the rate at which the *additive* enters the tank is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Q}_{\\text{in}}^{′} & =(0.03\\,\\frac{\\text{kg}}{\\text{L}})\\cdot (10\\,\\frac{\\text{L}}{\\text{min}}) \\\\  & =(0.03\\,\\frac{\\text{kg}}{\\cancel{\\text{L}}})\\cdot (10\\,\\frac{\\cancel{\\text{L}}}{\\text{min}}) \\\\  & =0.3\\,\\frac{\\text{kg}}{\\text{min}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Calculating the rate at which additive exits the tank.\n\nNext, note that the rate of flow in equals the rate of flow out, so the volume in the tank remains $800\\,\\text{L}.$ Then, since $Q$ is the amount of additive in the tank, the *concentration* of the solution at time $t$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{Q}{800}\\,\\text{kg/L}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, as the completely mixed liquid leaves at a rate of $10\\,\\text{L/min},$ *additive* leaves at a rate of\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Q}_{\\text{out}}^{′} & =(10\\,\\frac{\\text{L}}{\\text{min}})\\cdot (\\frac{Q}{800}\\,\\frac{\\text{kg}}{\\text{L}}) \\\\  & =(10\\,\\frac{\\cancel{\\text{L}}}{\\text{min}})\\cdot (\\frac{Q}{800}\\,\\frac{\\text{kg}}{\\cancel{\\text{L}}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{10Q}{800}\\,\\frac{\\text{kg}}{\\text{min}} \\\\  & =\\frac{Q}{80}\\,\\frac{\\text{kg}}{\\text{min}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Calculate the overall rate of change.\n\nThe rate of change equals the rate of entry minus the rate of exit. Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dQ}{dt} & ={Q}_{\\text{in}}^{′}-{Q}_{\\text{out}}^{′} \\\\  & =0.3-\\frac{Q}{80}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dQ}{dt}+\\frac{1}{80}Q=0.3.\n$$\n\n**Step 4**: Integrate the equation.\n\nThis is a first-order linear equation with constant coefficients. To find the general solution, we must sum the complementary and particular solutions.\n\n- To find the complementary solution ${Q}_{c},$ we solve the corresponding homogeneous equation, given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{d{Q}_{c}}{dt}+\\frac{1}{80}{Q}_{c}=0.\n$$\n\nSolving using an integration technique, such as separation of variables, we obtain the complementary solution\n\n$$\n{Q}_{c}(t)=A{e}^{-t/80},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is a constant of integration.\n\n- Next, we find the particular solution. Note that the right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is a polynomial of degree $0.$ So, we assume that the particular solution is also a polynomial of degree $0,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{Q}_{p}(t)=\\alpha .\n$$\n\nTo find the value of $\\alpha ,$ we substitute ${Q}_{p}=\\alpha $ and $\\frac{d{Q}_{p}}{dt}=(\\alpha )^{′}=0$ into the inhomogeneous equation:\n\n$$\n0+\\frac{1}{80}\\alpha =0.3\\,⟹\\,\\alpha =24.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution is ${Q}_{p}(t)=24.$\n\nNow, since the general solution is given by the sum of the complementary solution and the particular solution, the general solution in our case is\n\n$$\nQ(t)={Q}_{c}(t)+{Q}_{p}(t)=A{e}^{-t/80}+24.\n$$\n\nWe're told that the tank initially contains $15\\,\\text{kg}$ of dissolved additive. So, we can apply the initial condition $Q(0)=15,$ and solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(0) & =15 \\\\ A{e}^{-0/80}+24 & =15 \\\\ A & =-9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following expression for $Q(t):$\n\n$$\nQ(t)=24-9{e}^{-t/80}.\n$$"] [:db/add "79b642d6-727a-5f0d-9531-4fcd626dce40" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] [:db/add "79b642d6-727a-5f0d-9531-4fcd626dce40" :question/answer-fields "4cab0c71-5a81-5ddc-9dfe-02c242f74b7b"] [:db/ensure "79b642d6-727a-5f0d-9531-4fcd626dce40" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186229181 :knowledge-point/questions "79b642d6-727a-5f0d-9531-4fcd626dce40"] [:db/add "generator" :question-generator/id #uuid "ff33eaa5-573d-5d81-96ae-0be6c7033952"] [:db/add "generator" :question-generator/script "generators/69/693c8cfb9fad7a2f463430dcdb63d06593ec1b5b90cfb1410378472b5cb0c1c3/17592186229181.py"] [:db/add 17592186229181 :knowledge-point/question-generator "generator"] [:db/ensure 17592186229181 :knowledge-point/validate]]
